@startuml 01a-use-cases-overview
!include style.iuml
title Use cases, overview: actors and the five packages
left to right direction

actor "Owner" as Owner
actor "Product manager" as PM
actor "Coordinator" as Coord
actor "Engineer" as Eng
actor "Claude Code session" as CC
actor "GitHub (gh CLI)" as GH <<external system>>
actor "Clock (timer)" as Clock <<internal>>

rectangle "opencode-coordination" {
  usecase "Communication\n(ask, answer, note, record,\nhistory, owner order, safety, incident)" as P1
  usecase "Work control\n(propose, accept, breakdown, assign,\nclaim, progress, ready, verdict, hold)" as P2
  usecase "Progress control\n(decide, prioritize, measure, validate,\nboard, state digest, bundle, render)" as P3
  usecase "History\n(append event, export, import, rebuild)" as P4
  usecase "Automations\n(PR sync, reminders, escalation, stalls,\nidle, gone, prompt, title, names)" as P5
}

PM --> P1
Coord --> P1
Eng --> P1
CC --> P1
Coord --> P2
Eng --> P2
PM --> P2 : propose only
PM --> P3
Coord --> P3 : answer decisions,\nstate digest, board
Eng --> P3 : result only
Owner <-- P3 : bundle, pages
Owner --> P1 : orders any session
GH --> P5
Clock --> P5
P1 ..> P4 : <<include>>
P2 ..> P4 : <<include>>
P3 ..> P4 : <<include>>
P5 ..> P4 : <<include>>
P5 ..> P1 : <<include>>\ndelivers reminders\nand digests
P5 ..> P2 : <<include>>\nmoves items on\nmerge, gone, unclaimed

note bottom of P4
  One actor per event, written by the plugin
  from the authenticated session. Nothing is pruned.
end note
@enduml
